 "text": "Hi! How's everything today? About three to four weeks before. Plants don't like surprises, so give them a gentle nudge the same time every year. Then look at your local weather forecast for the day you want them gone. Pull them rather than cut them so you don't scorch stems. Both are fine. Texting is quick way if you' short on time, and some people prefer it because it' not so final. That's lovely. Frame it with the real flower buds from last year, so she has a keepsake too. Keep them simple and friendly. Hi and a short greeting are fine, and add the date and who it' from at the top.",
